#ClipThat

Super lightweight clipboard manager for windows written in C using Wind32 and SQLite3

ClipThat runs in system tray, keeps the copy entries into a database for later use.

## Features

1. Clipboard History
2. Duplicate Detection
3. Most Recently Used History Ordering
4. Configurable history limit
5. System Tray
6. Global Hotkey ( CTRL + ALT + H )
7. Double Click to restore and paste
8. SQLite Presistance
9. UFT-16 clipboard support
10. No External runtime dependencies

## Current Ver

**V 1.0.0**

## How it works
Clipboard changes are captured through the Windows clipboard listener API, during runtime clipboard entries are stored in memory as a linked list:

Clipboard -> Win32 clipboard listener -> History manager -> In-memory linked list -> History UI

When the application shuts down, the current history is written to SQLite, on the next launch, the history is loaded back into memory


## Database

The database is created automatically after opening the ClipThat which will be stored in %LOCALAPPDATA%\ClipThat\

## Hotkey usage
 
for showing history you have to use Ctrl + Alt + H or you can use the tray icon, you have to right click on it and a menu will show up which there you can open the history or exit the program.

## Building 
### Requirements
for building you need {
    Windows OS (OBV !!)
    Visual studio
    Desktop Development with c++ workload
    Windows SDK
}

even tho the program is written in C you still need the c++ workload in Visual Studio.

